Referring to a specific function of the used libraries can sometimes be 
cumbersome to type and read considering the additional prefix. 
This can be simplified by adding those to the local namespace with using.
Be careful when applying using namespace, as it brings many functions and 
variables to the scope of the program. Thereby conflicts with your own symbols 
of functions and variables may occur.
(Please note: the comma separated list in using requires at least C++17.)

