Whether you use c or C++, dynamic memory allocation uses different commands.
The result is the same.
Please note: the first printf statement can lead to a program crash as the pointer
p is not initialized and my point to areas outside the allocated memory space.
Sometimes variables are automatically initialized to zero - accessing the address
zero also results in a crash.

