[Sedgewick, Algorithmen in C++]
set_union is a method to create the union of two sets.
It requires the first and last element of the two sources as well as an iterator
pointing to the next position for insertion.
The input sets have to occur in a sorted fashion when iterating through them.
Related operations are the difference of sets and their intersection.
The method merge combines both input sets including duplicates. To see this
effect, the target container has to be a vector as duplicates get automatically
removed in a set.

