142
The class name itself acts as constructor, which is called when an object of that 
class is created. When the object is deleted, the deconstructor method is called, 
which has a preceding ‘~’ in front of the class name.
In this example, we use polymorphism to enable variations of the created object –
a default way and one that provides a specific status. Constructor and 
deconstructor can be omitted if nothing is to be done on creation or deletion of an 
object.
The shown example highlights the concept of the scope of objects and their 
automatic deletion, once they leave a scope. Leaving the function sub results in 
an automatic call of the deconstrutor of the object stored in pers (which is of the 
Member class).

